%%{init: {'theme':'neutral', 'sequence': {'mirrorActors': false}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor A as Admin
  participant B as Browser
  participant F as Flask app
  participant M as MongoDB Atlas

  rect rgb(243,246,252)
  Note over A,M: 1. Register an NGO account
  A->>B: Fill in NGO registration form
  B->>F: POST /register-ngo
  F->>F: Check role is admin, validate fields and password
  F->>M: users.find_one(email)
  M-->>F: no existing account
  F->>M: users.insert_one(role ngo, ngo_details)
  F->>M: audit_logs.insert_one(register-ngo)
  F-->>B: Flash "NGO account created"
  end

  rect rgb(246,250,243)
  Note over A,M: 2. View platform statistics
  A->>B: Open admin dashboard, pick year
  B->>F: GET /admin-dashboard?year=2026
  F->>F: Check role is admin
  F->>M: Aggregate donations, campaigns and users by month and role
  M-->>F: totals, trends, top campaigns
  F-->>B: Render admin-dashboard.html with charts
  end

  rect rgb(252,247,240)
  Note over A,M: 3. Send an announcement
  A->>B: Write subject, message, pick audience
  B->>F: GET /updates/audience
  F->>M: users.count_documents(by role)
  M-->>F: audience sizes
  F-->>B: Audience options
  B->>F: POST /updates/send
  F->>F: Check daily announcement limit, clean message
  F->>M: users.find(audience) to get recipients
  F->>M: updates.insert_one(kind announcement)
  F->>M: audit_logs.insert_one
  F-->>B: "Sent to N people"
  B-->>A: Announcement appears in Updates feed
  end

  rect rgb(250,243,250)
  Note over A,M: 4. Review the audit log and remove a user
  A->>B: Open audit log
  B->>F: GET /admin-audit
  F->>M: audit_logs.find + users.aggregate (activity)
  M-->>F: log entries
  F-->>B: Render admin_audit.html
  A->>B: Remove a user account with a reason
  B->>F: POST /admin/users/<user_id>/remove
  F->>M: users.update_one(account removed) + campaigns.update_many(owner_removed)
  F->>M: audit_logs.insert_one(remove)
  F-->>B: Flash "Account removed"
  end
